Description: define _STAT_VER fallback for modern host glibc

fakeroot 1.20.2 (bundled by this 2019-era Buildroot tree) expects
glibc's <bits/stat.h> to expose the _STAT_VER* macros. glibc >= ~2.32
dropped them from public headers as part of unifying 32/64-bit stat
internally (the ABI value didn't change, just the visibility). This
only affects the HOST build machine's fakeroot binary (used during
rootfs packaging), never anything that ships to the ARM target --
confirmed hit on this dev machine's glibc 2.36 (Debian 12).

Restores the historic per-arch glibc values as a fallback only when
the macro isn't already defined by the host's own headers, so this
is a no-op on older hosts that still provide it.

--- a/libfakeroot.c
+++ b/libfakeroot.c
@@ -59,6 +59,24 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "communicate.h"

+/* glibc >= 2.32-ish dropped the public _STAT_VER* macros from
+   <bits/stat.h> as part of unifying 32/64-bit stat internally; this
+   fakeroot release (1.20.2, bundled by this 2019-era Buildroot tree)
+   still expects them to exist on the host build machine. Restore the
+   historic glibc values (unchanged ABI-wise, just no longer exposed)
+   so this host tool still compiles on a modern host toolchain -- this
+   only affects the x86_64 build-machine binary, never anything that
+   ships to the ARM target. */
+#ifndef _STAT_VER
+#if defined(__x86_64__)
+#define _STAT_VER 1
+#elif defined(__aarch64__)
+#define _STAT_VER 0
+#else
+#define _STAT_VER 3
+#endif
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __APPLE__
 /* The *xattr functions are currently disabled on __APPLE__ since the prototypes
    are all different from the Linux versions and there is, as of yet, no
